    posthog.init('{{ env.posthogToken }}', {
        api_host: '{{ env.posthogHost }}',
        defaults: '2026-05-30',
        person_profiles: 'identified_only', // or 'always' to create profiles for anonymous users as well
    })
  </script>
  {%- endif %}
</head>
<body>

<a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a>

<header class="site-header">
  <div class="site-header__inner">
    <a href="/" class="site-logo">
      {#- The seal (BL-059). A snare drum in elevation, not the ring-and-dots
          mark it replaced — that geometry read as a vinyl label. Shell fills
          with currentColor (--accent via .site-logo__seal); head, rods and lug
          casings inherit fill: var(--gold). Same shape as
          /assets/img/seal.svg, which hard-codes the same token values because
          a favicon has no cascade to inherit from. -#}
      <svg class="site-logo__seal" viewBox="0 0 32 32" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
        <rect x="1" y="13.7" width="2.8" height="4.6" rx="1.3" />
        <rect x="28.2" y="13.7" width="2.8" height="4.6" rx="1.3" />
        <path d="M3.6 9.4V22.6a12.4 4.4 0 0 0 24.8 0V9.4Z" fill="currentColor" />
        <rect x="7.15" y="9.8" width="2.9" height="14.1" rx="1.45" />
        <rect x="14.55" y="9.8" width="2.9" height="15.4" rx="1.45" />
        <rect x="21.95" y="9.8" width="2.9" height="14.1" rx="1.45" />
        <path d="M3.6 22.6a12.4 4.4 0 0 0 24.8 0" fill="none" stroke="var(--gold)" stroke-width="2.6" />
        <ellipse cx="16" cy="9.4" rx="12.4" ry="4.4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" />
      </svg>
      <span class="site-logo__wm">drum<em>.town</em></span>
    </a>
    {#- Current-section highlight. Lesson pages pass navSection (foundations |
        track | mastery); everything else is derived from the URL. -#}
    {%- set sec = navSection or (
          'track' if '/genres/' in page.url else (
          'rudiments' if '/rudiments/' in page.url else (
          'metronome' if '/metronome/' in page.url else ''))) %}
    <nav class="site-nav" id="site-nav" aria-label="Site">
      <a href="/#foundations"{% if sec == 'foundations' %} class="active" aria-current="true"{% endif %}>Foundations</a>
      <a href="/#tracks"{% if sec == 'track' %} class="active" aria-current="true"{% endif %}>Genres</a>
      <a href="/#mastery"{% if sec == 'mastery' %} class="active" aria-current="true"{% endif %}>Other Topics</a>
      <a href="/rudiments/"{% if sec == 'rudiments' %} class="active" aria-current="page"{% endif %}>Rudiments</a>
      <a href="/metronome/"{% if sec == 'metronome' %} class="active" aria-current="page"{% endif %}>Metronome</a>
    </nav>
    <button class="theme-toggle" id="theme-toggle" type="button" aria-label="Switch to dark theme">
      <svg class="theme-toggle__sun" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
        <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="4.6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" />
        <g stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round">
          <path d="M12 2.4v2.6M12 19v2.6M2.4 12h2.6M19 12h2.6M5.2 5.2l1.9 1.9M16.9 16.9l1.9 1.9M18.8 5.2l-1.9 1.9M7.1 16.9l-1.9 1.9" />
        </g>
      </svg>
      <svg class="theme-toggle__moon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
        <path d="M20.5 14.6A8.6 8.6 0 1 1 9.4 3.5a7 7 0 0 0 11.1 11.1z" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linejoin="round" />
      </svg>
    </button>
    {#- Collapsed state of the transport dock (system.md §3/§7). Live BPM and
        time signature are written here by metronome.js; the lamp pulses with
        the beat so a running metronome is never hidden.

        The lamp carries no glyph (BL-074). It used to wear ▶ when stopped and ■
        when running, but pressing this button does neither — it opens and closes
        the dock, and a beginner who tapped the triangle got a drawer containing a
        second, identical triangle. The lamp is now a pure indicator (ring =
        stopped, filled = running, brass offbeat, brick downbeat) and the
        disclosure is carried by the chevron, which flips off the same
        aria-expanded this button already publishes — CSS only, no second source
        of truth in JS. -#}
    <button class="clock-pill" id="metronome-pill" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="site-metronome">
      <span class="clock-pill__dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <b class="clock-pill__bpm" aria-hidden="true">80</b><small class="clock-pill__sig" aria-hidden="true">· 4/4</small><span class="clock-pill__chev" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      {#- The whole accessible name lives in this one span rather than being
          concatenated from the visible parts: nothing separates <b> from the
          span in the rendered markup, so a composed name would run together as
          "80beats per minute". metronome.js rewrites the tempo and the running
          word here; open/closed is carried by aria-expanded, not by this text.
          The static wording below is the no-JS fallback. -#}
      <span class="sr-only" id="metronome-pill-state">Metronome, 80 beats per minute, stopped</span>
    </button>
    <button class="nav-toggle" id="nav-toggle" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="site-nav" aria-label="Menu">
      <span class="nav-toggle__bars" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    </button>
  </div>
</header>

<main id="main">
{{ content | safe }}
</main>

{#- Footer — the notice board (system.md §4). Four columns at desktop, 2 at
    820px, 1 at 560px with the identity block first. Every figure on the base
    line is computed from the data files at build time, never typed: the
    counts move when the curriculum does. -#}
{%- set rudimentCount = 0 %}
{%- for group in rudiments %}{% set rudimentCount = rudimentCount + group.rudiments.length %}{% endfor %}
<footer class="site-footer">
  <div class="site-footer__grid">
    <div class="site-footer__id">
      <svg class="site-footer__seal" viewBox="0 0 32 32" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
        <rect x="1" y="13.7" width="2.8" height="4.6" rx="1.3" />
        <rect x="28.2" y="13.7" width="2.8" height="4.6" rx="1.3" />
        <path d="M3.6 9.4V22.6a12.4 4.4 0 0 0 24.8 0V9.4Z" fill="currentColor" />
        <rect x="7.15" y="9.8" width="2.9" height="14.1" rx="1.45" />
        <rect x="14.55" y="9.8" width="2.9" height="15.4" rx="1.45" />
        <rect x="21.95" y="9.8" width="2.9" height="14.1" rx="1.45" />
        <path d="M3.6 22.6a12.4 4.4 0 0 0 24.8 0" fill="none" stroke="var(--gold)" stroke-width="2.6" />
        <ellipse cx="16" cy="9.4" rx="12.4" ry="4.4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" />
      </svg>
      {#- The one sanctioned poetry zone on the site (system.md §10). -#}
      <p class="site-footer__motto">The door's open. Bring sticks.</p>
      <p class="site-footer__fine">A free town for learning the drums. No accounts, no sign-ups — your progress lives in your own browser.</p>
    </div>
    {#- aria-labelledby rather than aria-label: the heading is already the
        column's name, and a duplicate string would have screen readers
        announce "Lessons navigation, heading, Lessons". -#}
    <nav class="site-footer__col" aria-labelledby="footer-nav-lessons">
      <h2 class="site-footer__h" id="footer-nav-lessons">Lessons</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/#foundations">Foundations</a></li>
        <li><a href="/#tracks">Genre tracks</a></li>
        <li><a href="/#mastery">Other topics</a></li>
      </ul>
    </nav>
    <nav class="site-footer__col" aria-labelledby="footer-nav-reference">
      <h2 class="site-footer__h" id="footer-nav-reference">Reference</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/rudiments/">The {{ rudimentCount }} rudiments</a></li>
        <li><a href="/metronome/">The metronome</a></li>
      </ul>
    </nav>
    <nav class="site-footer__col" aria-labelledby="footer-nav-town">
      <h2 class="site-footer__h" id="footer-nav-town">The town</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="https://github.com/dylanpjenkins/drum-town">GitHub</a></li>
        <li><a href="/lessons/{{ curriculum.foundations.sections[0].lessons[0].slug }}/">Start at lesson one</a></li>
      </ul>
    </nav>
  </div>
  <p class="site-footer__base">drum.town · {{ curriculum | lessonCount }} lessons · {{ lessonContent | exerciseCount }} playable exercises · {{ rudimentCount }} rudiments · notation rendered with VexFlow at build time · built on Eleventy</p>
</footer>

{#- Transport dock (system.md §7). Ships collapsed so no dock flashes open
    before metronome.js runs; the header clock pill expands it. Control IDs are
    unchanged from the old floating card — metronome.js keeps its wiring.

    Every control sits in a `.transport__field` whose `.transport__cap` names it
    in words (BL-075). At 390px the whole dock used to read "▶ ♪ ▾": the BPM
    label was display:none below 400px, so the tempo box was a naked "80", and
    the two sliders were unlabelled — one tempo, one volume, and you had to
    guess. The caps ride in the dead vertical space each 44px control already
    has above its own content, so the dock's height is unchanged and the reserve
    that tools/checks/check-transport-reserve.js enforces still holds. DOM order
    is unchanged too: the ≤720px two-row arrangement is driven by `order`, and
    the desktop row follows this source order.

    Each caption names its OWN control and nothing else. The dot row's caption
    read "Metronome" for one review cycle, on the theory that this field had the
    spare width to carry the dock's title; that was the same false affordance as
    the pill's old play triangle, one layer down — a beginner hunting for the word
    "metronome" found it, tapped it, and got nothing, because the field under it
    is decoration. It says "Beat" now, and the select next to it says "Meter"
    rather than "Beats", which also stops the row asserting that 6/8 has six
    beats. The dock has no visible title as a result; a title needs a treatment
    that is not a control caption, and that is filed separately. -#}
<aside class="transport is-collapsed" id="site-metronome" aria-label="Metronome">
  <div class="transport__row">
    <button class="transport__go" id="metronome-toggle" type="button" aria-label="Start metronome">
      <span class="transport__icon" aria-hidden="true">▶</span>
    </button>
    {#- Every caption is aria-hidden and every control keeps a single aria-label,
        so there is exactly one accessible name per control and the visible word
        is a substring of it — WCAG 2.5.3 is string containment, so a voice-control
        user saying "click BPM" has to land somewhere. All four pairs, in full:
          BPM     → "BPM, tempo in beats per minute"
          Tempo   → "Tempo slider"
          Meter   → "Meter, beats per bar"
          Volume  → "Volume"
        The BPM name gained its prefix here: "Tempo in beats per minute" does not
        contain the string "BPM", and while the visible label was display:none
        below 400px that was invisible as well as unspoken. A comma, not a dash —
        screen readers announce an em dash. The fifth caption, Beat, names the dot
        row, which is aria-hidden decoration and takes no name at all. -#}
    <label class="transport__field transport__bpm-wrap">
      <span class="transport__cap" aria-hidden="true">BPM</span>
      <input type="number" class="transport__bpm" id="metronome-bpm" value="80" min="30" max="240" step="1" aria-label="BPM, tempo in beats per minute" />
    </label>
    <label class="transport__field transport__tempo">
      <span class="transport__cap" aria-hidden="true">Tempo</span>
      <input type="range" class="transport__slider" id="metronome-slider" min="30" max="240" step="1" value="80" aria-label="Tempo slider" />
    </label>
    {#- A div, not a label, and deliberately: a <select> inside a <label> has a
        history of taking two taps on mobile browsers, because the label forwards
        a second click into the popup that just opened. Nothing is lost — the
        caption is aria-hidden either way and the select carries its own
        aria-label, and the select fills the field, so a tap on the caption still
        lands on the control underneath it. -#}
    <div class="transport__field transport__meter">
      <span class="transport__cap" aria-hidden="true">Meter</span>
      <select class="transport__timesig" id="metronome-timesig" aria-label="Meter, beats per bar">
        <option value="2">2/4</option>
        <option value="3">3/4</option>
        <option value="4" selected>4/4</option>
        <option value="5">5/4</option>
        <option value="6">6/8</option>
        <option value="7">7/8</option>
      </select>
    </div>
    <div class="transport__field transport__pulse">
      <span class="transport__cap" aria-hidden="true">Beat</span>
      {#- metronome.js rewrites this element's innerHTML on every time-signature
          change, so the caption has to be its sibling, not its child. -#}
      <div class="transport__beats" id="metronome-beats" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    </div>
    <label class="transport__field transport__vol">
      <span class="transport__cap" aria-hidden="true">Volume</span>
      <input type="range" class="transport__volume" id="metronome-volume" min="0" max="100" step="1" value="60" aria-label="Volume" />
    </label>
    <button class="transport__collapse" id="metronome-collapse" type="button" aria-expanded="true" aria-label="Collapse metronome">▾</button>
  </div>
</aside>

<script src="/assets/js/chrome.js" defer></script>
<script src="/assets/js/progress.js" defer></script>
<script src="/assets/js/pattern-math.js" defer></script>
<script src="/assets/js/player.js" defer></script>
<script src="/assets/js/metronome.js" defer></script>

</body>
</html>
